class Lesson(TypedDict):
    """A lesson page (S1.L1) or a drawer page (D-03), the two pages built from segments of blocks
    (ARCHITECTURE.md section 3.3 and section 17.3). Authors write its Markdown source
    (packages/content/README.md) and the content build parses it into this record; the derived
    fields (the rail, the cited runs, the revisions) are the build's.
    """
    schema: LessonSchemaTag
    # The lesson (S1.L1) or the drawer (D-03) this page is. The ID registry (generated from the
    # spine) must hold it, and the file name is the ID.
    id: LessonPageId
    # The lesson's tier in the spine's table: boot (S1.L0 only), core, bridge or step (S10.L1 to
    # S10.L7). Tier names stay internal: learners see plain formats. A drawer has no tier.
    tier: NotRequired[Literal["boot", "core", "bridge", "step"]]
    # The title, equal to the spine's title for the ID. One line.
    title: LessonLine
    # True while the page is unreviewed: it carries the label "draft: first-learner pass pending"
    # (spine section 13), and a run reference that does not resolve yet may wait. False once
    # learner-zero has studied the page and the owner has reviewed it, when every reference must
    # resolve (GATE-runs).
    draft: bool
    # The knowledge components the page teaches: a lesson's, the ones its items are tagged with; a
    # drawer's, the ones it teaches (the ones it only previews are in previews). Empty for a
    # deferred drawer, which has no graded item.
    kcs: list[LessonKcId]
    # A drawer only: the knowledge components it previews, which a lesson on the default path first
    # teaches later (curriculum/D-drawers.md section 1.5).
    previews: NotRequired[list[LessonKcId]]
    # The observable objective, in the learner's words.
    objective: NotRequired[LessonMd]
    # The drawers the page links beside its segments. A link is a line in the margin and in the
    # page's drawer list, never in the rail.
    drawers: NotRequired[list[LessonDrawerId]]
    # A deferred drawer only (D-30 to D-40): the card saying what the topic is, why the roadmap
    # defers it and what surfaces it. A deferred drawer has no segments and no graded item.
    deferred: NotRequired[LessonDeferred]
    # The segments, in order. The rail shows their titles and nothing else. A lesson has at least
    # one; a deferred drawer has none.
    segments: list[LessonSegment]
    # Derived: the sum of the segments' minutes.
    minutes: NotRequired[int]
    # Derived: the segment titles and nothing else, never an answer, a verdict or option text
    # (V2-05).
    rail: NotRequired[list[LessonRailEntry]]
    # Derived: the claims and specimens the page's claim and specimen blocks mint or show. The page
    # shows them only after its exit items (DESIGN.md section 6).
    establishes: NotRequired[LessonEstablishes]
    # Derived: every run the page cites, as the pruned record the run chip and the run sheet read,
    # by run ID. A draft's reference to a run that is not recorded yet has no entry here and is
    # listed in unresolved.
    runs: NotRequired[dict[str, LessonRunSnapshot]]
    # Derived: every registry fact the page cites with a fact reference, as the registry holds it,
    # by fact ID. The site prints the value and, once its TTL has passed, the "stale since" badge.
    facts: NotRequired[dict[str, LessonFactSnapshot]]
    # Derived: the title block's "Checked by", the engine and version of each cited run as the run
    # records them, with its run ID.
    checkedBy: NotRequired[list[LessonCheckedBy]]
    # Derived, drafts only: the run IDs the page cites that runs/ does not hold yet. A page that is
    # not a draft has none, or the build fails.
    unresolved: NotRequired[list[LessonRunId]]
    # Derived: SHA-256 over the page as built, which the title block's "Rev" shows.
    rev: NotRequired[Sha256]


# A stage, such as S1.
LessonStageId = str


