class Receipt(TypedDict):
    """statespace receipt, version 1

    The Bench's report of what real tools said about one lab stage (spine section 9.4;
    ARCHITECTURE.md section 10). statespace check and statespace trace validate write it to
    receipts/ in the learner's lab repository; INS-receipt imports it on the instrument origin,
    where it yields stamps and claims, never evidence of learning. A receipt never trusts an exit
    code alone: every runs[] entry carries the verdict lines verbatim, and the importer
    re-derives each verdict from them. A file may carry only the lanes reported (shown as
    reported from your machine) and self-assessed; only the tab assigns re-checked here, at read
    time, to checks it re-ran itself, so that badge is never stored in a receipt. Statement
    hashes follow statement-hash@1 (defs.schema.json), and a changed hash voids the claim to [?].
    The receipt version, the hash rule and the rule that versions are recorded verbatim never
    change in place (labs/TOOLS.md section 6.4). Fields are camelCase as spine section 9.4 writes
    them, except reason_unknown, which is Z3's own name.
    """
    schema: Literal["statespace/receipt@1"]
    # The lab, such as LAB-2.
    lab: LabId
    # The lab stage the receipt reports, such as LAB-2.2. It must belong to lab; the importer checks
    # that (ARCHITECTURE.md section 10.3, step 5).
    stage: LabStageId
    # reported (badge: reported from your machine) when the CLI ran the checks; self-assessed when
    # the learner judged them. re-checked here is not a value: the tab assigns it at read time and
    # never stores it.
    lane: Literal["reported", "self-assessed"]
    # When the CLI wrote the receipt.
    createdAt: Instant
    # The CLI that wrote the receipt.
    cli: ReceiptCli
    # Where the checks ran. The sandbox is recorded, never required (spine section 9.2).
    environment: ReceiptEnvironment
    # Every tool the checks ran, with its version verbatim and the SHA-256 of its binary, jar or
    # wheel.
    tools: list[ReceiptTool]
    # The pinned statements the checks were about, each with its statement hash (I7).
    statements: list[ReceiptStatement]
    # One entry per tool execution, in the order the CLI ran them.
    runs: list[ReceiptRun]
    lean: NotRequired[ReceiptLean]
    goldens: NotRequired[ReceiptGoldens]
    tlc: NotRequired[ReceiptTlc]
    z3: NotRequired[ReceiptZ3]
    pg: NotRequired[ReceiptPg]
    traces: NotRequired[ReceiptTraces]
    datalog: NotRequired[ReceiptDatalog]
    pairs: NotRequired[ReceiptPairs]
    # The stage's checks and whether each passed. Every id belongs to lab (ARCHITECTURE.md section
    # 10.3, step 5).
    checks: list[ReceiptCheck]
    provenance: ReceiptProvenance
    # The claim cards to mint or update in the lab repository, by template or by the learner's id.
    claims: NotRequired[list[ReceiptClaim]]
    # The trusted computing base of the stage's guarantee: each component and how it is backed.
    tcb: NotRequired[list[ReceiptTcbEntry]]
    # A Sigstore attestation; absent by default (OD-13).
    attestation: NotRequired[dict[str, Any]]
    # Forward-compatible extras. The stamp deriver ignores them.
    ext: NotRequired[dict[str, Any]]


